<title>MONGOLIA: Mongolia flour imports tripled in Jan-Oct.</title>
<headline>Mongolia flour imports tripled in Jan-Oct.</headline>
<dateline>ULAN BATOR 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mongolia tripled its imports of wheat flour to 75,494 tonnes in January-October from 25,000 tonnes in the same period in 1995, customs data showed on Tuesday.</p>
<p>China accounted for the bulk of the flour at 70,436 tonnes while Russia provided 2,477 tonnes and the Czech Republic 1,548 tonnes.</p>
<p>The Ministry of Agriculture and Industry said imports had increased because of a poor wheat harvest and reduced domestic flour production this year.</p>
</text>
